Do you need to install MongoDB and Redis separately?

No, not necessarily.

You can run both using Docker containers. This keeps your Ubuntu installation cleaner and makes it easier to configure different environments for your assignments.

For example, you can run Redis using:

docker run -d \
  --name redis-server \
  -p 6379:6379 \
  redis:7

Check whether Redis is working:

docker exec redis-server redis-cli ping

Expected output:
PONG

You can later use Docker Compose to configure the more complex environments required by your assignments.
